## 1. Executive Summary

MedSync Health, a leading digital health platform, delivered a strong start to the fiscal year 2024, continuing its trajectory of high revenue growth and strategic market penetration. Revenue for the first quarter of 2024 reached **AED 110.25 million**, representing a significant year-over-year growth of **36.4%** compared to Q1 2023. This growth was primarily driven by the continued success of the flagship **MedSync Connect** product and the accelerating adoption of the **MedSync Compliance Suite**.

While the company remains in a strategic investment phase, focusing on R&D and market expansion ahead of its planned Series D funding round, the gross margin remained robust at **75.0%**. Operating loss for the quarter was contained at **AED 4.48 million**, reflecting planned investments in product development and sales infrastructure. Key customer metrics, such as a Net Revenue Retention (NRR) of **118%** and an LTV:CAC ratio of **10.7x**, underscore the strong unit economics and long-term value of the customer base.

